        "content": "<p>Currently, we have some declarations which use <code>not_unit</code> in their name to refer to <code>¬IsUnit</code>. Should these be changed to <code>not_isUnit</code> to follow the naming convention? See for example, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Prime.not_unit#doc\">docs#Prime.not_unit</a> vs <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Irreducible.not_isUnit#doc\">docs#Irreducible.not_isUnit</a>.</p>",
